<title>FINLAND: FORECAST-Aamulehti 1996 profit seen up.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Aamulehti 1996 profit seen up.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Reuters survey of analysts covering Finnish equities showed a 105 million markka median forecast for Finnish publishing group Aamulehti Oy's full-year 1996 profit before extraordinary items and tax.</p>
<p>		   Profit before extras, tax	  EPS</p>
<p>			   (FIM million)		(markka)</p>
<p>    Median		   105			  9.40</p>
<p>    Mean		     111			  9.60</p>
<p>    Lowest		   100			  7.70</p>
<p>    Highest		  151			 12.50</p>
<p>(Profit forecasts by 11 analysts, EPS by nine analysts) @</p>
<p>Aamulehti's results are due on Feb 13.</p>
<p>In 1995, Aamulehti had a 87 million markka profit before extraordinary items and tax.</p>
<p>For the company's full-year 1997 profit, seven of the 11 analysts polled gave a median forecast of 115 million markka (mean 120 million) in a 95 to 149 million markka range.</p>
<p>Contributors to the survey were Alfred Berg, Aktia Bank, Carnegie Securities, Erik Selin, Evli Securities, FIM Securities, Interbank, Kleinwort Benson Securities, Merita Securities, Opstock and Postipankki.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 6805 0240</p>
